Z||000005||Leadfoot||06-19-2001||06:55 PM||||     I know what you mean.  Everyone of friends and their cousins have some goofy question like "aren't those the cars that catch on fire?"  Makes you want to smack them. My old man is the worst though.  He kept saying he wouldn't go for a spin in my 85 SE cause it is too dangerous.  Cripes! he's almost 60, he's already got one foot in the grave and the other on a banana peel.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>     I was looking at oliver scholz's top ten lists and I noticed he didn't have a category titled: "Top Ten Stupid Questions Fiero Owners are Asked."  So far I can think of at least 20. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>     One of the dumbest questions came from my girlfriends brother.  The guy owns an 98 corvete and asks me if I have to replace my muffler on a regular basis....what the F***!  This coming from someone whose car is so low that if he backed over a credit card his wheels would come off the ground.<BR>    Fiero owners rule!!<BR>||||reg||7
