Z||000010||Formula88||06-19-2001||08:16 PM||||Well, my dad finally got to see my Fiero for the first time on Father's Day.  He thought it was cool, cuz it reminded him of his 61 Corvair (engine in the back, and all).  As for one foot in the grave, he's 75, so don't think "almost" 60's getting old.  My mom digs the car too.  As for the ladies... one special lady friend of mine thought the car was awesome, till she drove it.  Now she thinks it's incredible!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I love girls who are into cars.  Not enough of 'em around here.  Of course, she's also the type to put Pirelli P7000 Supersports on her Civic cuz she doesn't like to slow down for corners!  Oh, and it's totally stock, with no stickers or other rice sh!t anywhere.  We're thinking about, when that engine finally dies, putting an Integra Type R engine in it, but keeping it looking stock on the outside.  She likes sleepers, too!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||06-20-2001||11:45 AM||||ok we need some stock answers to these stupid questions so they pop up right in our minds (like arnie in the Terminator) when the opportunity arises<P> Isnt this the car that catches on fire?<P>Ans: Yes but dont worry, Ive replaced all the flammible material with either abspestos or fiberglass (then see how long till they jump up out of the fiberglass/abspestos seat).<P>Q: are we gonna die in here?<P>A: Im hoping I will.<P>A: I can make you feel like you've died and gone to heaven.<P>Q: I heard these cars are dangerous!<P>A: Not anywhere as dangerous as me, baby!||||reg||1
