Z||000030||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||06:59 AM||||Q: Is this thing gonna fall apart with us in it?<P>A: no, it kinda shakes itselfs apart.<P>BTW autotrader.com or one of those car selling websites has links to the safety ratings of used car. For driver and passenger safety in a collision, the fiero, from 84 to 88 was rated excellent, their highest rating.<P>Q: is this car safe?<P>A: The saturn, one of the safest cars in the world, was patterned after the Fiero, taking advantage of the 5 years of experience General Motors accumulated with production of its space frame construction - in fact, the space frame of the Saturn is lighter than the one you are sitting in now because the engineers felt this car was over-design - and furthermore blah blah blah blah blah ...||||reg||1
