Z||000034||Ken Wittlief||06-21-2001||09:18 AM||||Kyle is a new fiero owner - I didnt know fieros weight 2600 lbs and had a spaceframe when I first started looking for one till someone on this forum told me.<P>  In fact back then, I saw a fiero on ebay with a V8 in it, and thought, is this guys nuts?!?! I thought a fiero was a small light car designed for a 4 cylinder engine with cheap suspension - and that putting a V8 in it was just plain stupid.<P>  took me a while to understand how solid they are, how much they can be modified, and that even the suspension can be upgraded.<P>  to be fair to all the people with bad opinions of fieros, go look in one of the older edmunds or similar used car guides - they tell you to stay away from fieros, and only the 88 GTs or Forumulas are worth owning - the rest are in the 'do not buy for any reason' column.<P>   Personally I kinda like the bad rep fieros have - if they were popular cars - like miatas for example, I would never be able to afford one. <P><BR>--- yeah! thats it! these cars are dangeous! you know anyone that has one? Tell them they shouldnt drive it - dont let their kids drive it - give me their phone number and I will tow it away for them and have it properly dismantled<P>  (and restored -hehehe (c%<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
